"given\": \"A status filter was selected before a request was opened.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows the Requests list with the previously selected filter still selected.\",\n     \"when\": \"The user follows the detail screen's Back link.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Hive Works Request detail screen shall show a Back link, the request title, area, priority badge, status badge, UTC creation date in date-only form, and the description or “No description.” when absent, and return to the Requests list with its previously selected filter retained when Back is followed.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A request is displayed with each of the statuses Open, In progress, or Done.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows Start work, Mark done, or Reopen respectively, and after a successful response the status badge and action button show the new status and next action.\",\n     \"when\": \"The detail screen renders and the user selects its status action, with the API confirming the change.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Hive Works Request detail screen shall show Start work for Open requests, Mark done for In progress requests, and Reopen for Done requests, and update the status badge and action button only after a successful status-change response.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The detail screen shows a request with a known status.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows “Could not update the request.” and the status badge and action button retain their previous values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API returns a failure for the status update.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a status update fails, then the Hive Works app shall show “Could not update the request.” and keep the previously displayed status and action unchanged.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The detail screen is opened with an unknown ID.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.\",\n     \"when\": \"The ID lookup completes.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The detail screen is opened with a known ID and loading fails for a non-not-found reason.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.2\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows a generic loading error and a Retry action, not “Request not found.”.\",\n     \"when\": \"The load failure is returned.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The detail screen shows a generic loading error.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.3\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen sends another request to load the detail address.\",\n     \"when\": \"The user selects Retry.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Hive Works app shall show “Request not found.” with a link back to the Requests screen for an unknown ID, and show a generic loading error with Retry but not “Request not found.” when loading a known ID fails for another reason.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The Requests and request detail screens are rendered with all badge types and primary buttons.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows the light theme, neutral background, near-black text, sans-serif font, one primary-button brand color, and the specified status and priority badge colors, with each badge showing its status or priority value.\",\n     \"when\": \"Their theme and badges are inspected.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Hive Works app shall use one light theme with a neutral background, near-black text, one primary-button brand color, one sans-serif font, Open blue badges, In progress amber badges, Done green badges, Urgent red badges, and neutral Low and Normal badges, with text on every badge.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The Requests, creation dialog, and detail screens are rendered at 375 px and 1280 px viewport widths.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-23.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows stacked request cards at 375 px, a request table at 1280 px, no horizontal page scroll, labels for every field, and keyboard-reachable controls.\",\n     \"when\": \"The screens and controls are inspected and navigated by keyboard.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Hive Works app shall present labeled fields and keyboard-reachable controls on both screens and provide stacked request cards at 375 px and a request table at 1280 px viewport widths without horizontal page scrolling.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"I-7\",\n    \"Q-10\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The automated business-rule test suite is available.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-24.1\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"The test report lists passing cases for a valid request starting Open, missing or too-short title, missing area, too-long description, each allowed status transition, a disallowed transition, a status-filtered newest-first list, and an unknown ID.\",\n     \"when\": \"The suite is run against the application API.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Hive Works project shall include automated tests for request creation and validation, all allowed and disallowed status transitions, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-ID handling.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The app is available to the end-to-end test.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-25.1\",\n     \"level\": \"ui\",\n     \"then\": \"The test report shows the workflow passed and the screen shows the created request in the Done list.\",\n     \"when\": \"The test opens the list, creates a request, opens it, selects Start work and Mark done, then filters by Done.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Hive Works project shall include an end-to-end test for the create, detail, status-change, and filter workflow.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-25\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  }\n ],\n \"roundTrip\": {\n  \"droppedSpans\": [],\n  \"inventedCapabilities\": []\n },\n \"settled\": [\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"How should the 25-requirement scope be handled for this run? → Approve all 25 requirements as one run.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"lint\",\n   \"problem\": \"L9 size: This spec has 25 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.\",\n   \"ref\": \"Q-9\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Should the 1280 px wide-layout viewport be a fixed requirement or configurable? → Keep 1280 px as a fixed required viewport width.\",\n   \"how\": \"answered\",\n   \"kind\": \"lint\",\n   \"problem\": \"L12 literals: REQ-23 hardcodes \\\"1280\\\"; should it be configuration?\",\n   \"ref\": \"Q-10\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"decision\": \"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk\",\n   \"how\": \"open-risk\",\n   \"kind\": \"critic\",\n   \"problem\": \"ASM-2 accepts a cloud-hosted deployment and the intent is tagged auth/pii, but no requirement covers who may call the unauthenticated create and change-status API once it is publicly reachable, so there is no permission path at all.\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-09T23:47:02.602Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261009-co-working-space-maintenance-0f9d\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": [\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-1\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-2\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-3\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-4\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-5\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-6\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-7\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-8\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"critic\" kind=\"critic\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"findings\": [\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The spec never says what happens to a description that is only whitespace: after trimming it is an empty string, but REQ-2 includes a description \\\"only if one was supplied\\\" and REQ-18 shows “No description.” only \\\"when absent\\\", so it is unclear whether \\\"\\\" is stored or shown.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Several ACs check the \\\"persisted row\\\" or \\\"database row\\\" (AC-2.1, AC-5.1, AC-6.1–6.3, AC-7.2, AC-10.1–10.4) instead of a public API or UI surface, so they can only be checked by inspecting the database directly.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-7.2 says only that an attempt to change title, area, priority or description is \\\"rejected\\\", without saying whether a change-status call that also carries those fields is rejected or ignored, or what response is returned.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The list operation accepts an \\\"optional single status\\\" filter, but no AC covers an unsupported or malformed filter value (an error response, or ignore and return all).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Status actions have no pending or disabled state, unlike Create in REQ-16, so a double-click on Start work can send two transitions where the second fails and shows “Could not update the request.” after a successful change.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"If the stored status was changed elsewhere (a stale detail screen), the transition is rejected and REQ-20 keeps showing the stale status and action with no refresh, so the user can never move forward without reloading.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"ASM-2 accepts a cloud-hosted deployment and the intent is tagged auth/pii, but no requirement covers who may call the unauthenticated create and change-status API once it is publicly reachable, so there is no permission path at all.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"ASM-2 (one cloud region in the client's account) does not appear in the spec's assumptions or any requirement, and both assumptions cite the wrong questions (ASM-1 cites Q-6, which is about seeding, and ASM-2 cites Q-7, which is about filters), so their traceability is broken.\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The EARS requires tests for \\\"all allowed and disallowed status transitions\\\", while AC-24.1 requires only \\\"a disallowed transition\\\", so the AC can pass while most disallowed transitions are untested.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-24\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-15.1 requires the new request \\\"at the top of the list\\\", but REQ-8/Q-3 make the order of equal timestamps unspecified, so the new request may legitimately not be first.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The EARS says \\\"four Open requests with one Urgent request\\\", while AC-6.1 says \\\"including an Urgent Open row\\\", which leaves open whether there must be exactly one Urgent seed row or at least one.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Seeding only when the database is empty has no guard against two instances initializing the same empty database at once, which would leave more than eight seed rows and break the \\\"exactly 8\\\" rule.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-1.2's \\\"the screen list contains no third screen\\\" points to no public surface that can be observed, and AC-1.1 combines rendering the list with opening a request in a single When.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 3,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"No AC says whether a malformed (non-existent-format) ID in the detail address is treated as “Request not found.” or as a generic loading error.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"rubric\": 2,\n   \"severity\": \"low\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"Validat